just five days now until the first group  of ccsd students are welcome back to  campus  and a major update from the district  this afternoon giving details on  opening plans for all grade levels good  afternoon thanks so much for joining us  at four i'm kirsten joyce  and i'm christian casares today district  leaders saying they plan to bring back  all students before the end of the  school year  for some type of in-person instruction 8  news now reporter kirsten drummond is  live outside peterson elementary school  with all the latest details kristin  kiersten and christian dr jesus jarv  revealing the reopening plans today at  this campus  for grade levels beyond pre-kindergarten  to third grade students  we want to lay out those dates so take a  look here this is the  timeline we know that some lower  elementary school students are returning  march 1st to a hybrid model  but the proposed timeline has all ccsd  employees back in buildings  no later than march 15. on march 22nd  grades 6 9 and 12 will likely return to  in-person learning under the hybrid  model that date is also april 6th for  grades 7  8 10 and 11. also on april 6 the  district wants pre-k through grade five  starting five days a week in person  learning so that means  fourth and fifth graders are coming back  likely on april 6th  and will not participate in hybrid  learning and that's where students  attend class  in person two days and remotely the  other three days in the week  doctor jarrah says the state easing  school opening restrictions last week  helped speed up the process  he adds the district chose 6th 9th and  12th grades first  for a reason you look at our sixth  graders that have not been in a school  in their middle schools all year and our  high school  uh ninth graders as well it was an  opportunity for us to get our kids in  for a week  to transition into our middle schools  and high school before our upperclassmen  showed up  it remains unknown if secondary schools  will transition to full-time  in-person learning five days a week  before the end of the school year  doctor jarrah says it depends on how  well safety and health strategies  are preventing the spread of kobit 19.  the agreement to reopen  all the grade levels still needs to be  reviewed by the unions  and of course the board of trustees  still need to approve it  reporting live in lost in las vegas  kristen drummond 8 news now
 

